ction polls are available, so the picture rests on fundamentals rather than surveys.\n\nMoney is lopsided: Hickenlooper has raised about $9.5 million to Baisley's roughly $138,000, with no outside spending against the incumbent. The main wrinkle is Bob Chew, a deep-pocketed independent who has put $3.6 million into the race; he could draw some votes but is not seen as a serious threat. October debates featured sharp clashes over Trump, fuel prices, and Social Security, and Hickenlooper has acknowledged voter anger, but nothing in the record points to a competitive race.", "history": [{"date": "2026-09-22", "p_dem": 0.9917, "margin": 17.12}, {"date": "2026-09-23", "p_dem": 0.9895, "margin": 17.0}, {"date": "2026-09-24", "p_dem": 0.9916, "margin": 17.0}, {"date": "2026-09-25", "p_dem": 0.987, "margin": 17.0}, {"date": "2026-09-26", "p_dem": 0.9886, "margin": 17.0}, {"date": "2026-09-27", "p_dem": 0.9878, "margin": 16.5}, {"date": "2026-09-28", "p_dem": 0.9912, "margin": 17.0}, {"date": "2026-09-29", "p_dem": 0.994, "margin": 17.0}, {"date": "2026-09-30", "p_dem": 0.9898, "margin": 17.0}, {"date": "2026-10-01", "p_dem": 0.9915, "margin": 17.0}, {"date": "2026-10-02", "p_dem": 0.9938, "margin": 17.0}, {"date": "2026-10-03", "p_dem": 0.9899, "margin": 17.0}, {"date": "2026-10-04", "p_dem": 0.9876, "margin": 16.5}, {"date": "2026-10-05", "p_dem": 0.989, "margin": 17.2}, {"date": "2026-10-06", "p_dem": 0.9887, "margin": 17.0}, {"date": "2026-10-07", "p_dem": 0.9898, "margin": 17.0}, {"date": "2026-10-08", "p_dem": 0.9905, "margin": 17.0}, {"date": "2026-10-09", "p_dem": 0.989, "margin": 17.3}, {"date": "2026-10-10", "p_dem": 0.9875, "margin": 17.0}, {"date": "2026-10-11", "p_dem": 0.9898, "margin": 17.0}, {"date": "2026-10-12", "p_dem": 0.9916, "margin": 17.0}, {"date": "2026-10-13", "p_dem": 0.9925, "margin": 17.0}, {"date": "2026-10-14", "p_dem": 0.9877, "margin": 17.0}, {"date": "2026-10-15", "p_dem": 0.9883, "margin": 17.2}, {"date": "2026-10-16", "p_dem": 0.9849, "mar